THE FINDING, MADE AGAIN, and wider than the reader gave it. The reader names two numbers of patch 10's note that
no test holds. Each of the note's nine numbers was changed on the page in turn and the lock run: five passed, not
two. The first derivation's "120 of 120" and "88 of 120" (likely the reader's two), and the second derivation's
√5/2, √2 and 17/12. The other four (1,332 of 1,332; 358 or 362; 3,378; 1.4866) were held.

THE MEND. One test, added to the lock. The first derivation's sentence is built from the run's own numbers (the
count of matrices, the agreement at the marks that annihilate their own line, the one agreement at each of the
other four) and looked for on the page. The second derivation's sentence is held as it stands, with the values
that the lock's test of the second least reading computes. The test plants each of the five changes and sees
it reported.

The five plants, made on the page: each passed the lock before this patch, and each fails it now. The lock: 15
passed. Not checked by main.
---
 .../test_b1895_the_mends_of_b1881_read.py     | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/frontier/B1895_the_mends_of_b1881_read_and_what_its_second_convention_is/verification/test_b1895_the_mends_of_b1881_read.py b/frontier/B1895_the_mends_of_b1881_read_and_what_its_second_convention_is/verification/test_b1895_the_mends_of_b1881_read.py
index fc98703f2..a47af4dc0 100644
--- a/frontier/B1895_the_mends_of_b1881_read_and_what_its_second_convention_is/verification/test_b1895_the_mends_of_b1881_read.py
+++ b/frontier/B1895_the_mends_of_b1881_read_and_what_its_second_convention_is/verification/test_b1895_the_mends_of_b1881_read.py
@@ -410,3 +410,29 @@ def test_the_keys_of_a_verdict_file_are_read():
     assert _uncorrected(name, json.dumps({o1 + " [" + mark + "]": "a value"})) == (0, 1)      # the twin
     assert _uncorrected(name, json.dumps({"a key": {"a deeper key": [o1]}})) == (1, 1)      # values at any depth, as before
 
+
+def test_the_note_on_row_a1_gives_the_numbers_the_run_and_the_lock_compute():
+    """ADDED 2026-11-13 (C16; a cold reader's finding on R80b's part 2, patch 10, not checked by main, made again first).  The
+    note of 2026-11-12 under row A1 states two derivations, and the lock held four of their numbers: changed on the page, the
+    other five passed (the first derivation's 120 of 120 and 88 of 120; the second's √5/2, √2 and 17/12).  Each is held now by
+    a sentence built from the run, or, for the second derivation's three, by the sentence whose values
+    test_the_second_least_reading_is_the_all_twos_over_the_cyclic_sequences_that_were_read computes."""
+    a = RES["A_numbers"]
+    words = {2: "two", 4: "four"}
+    others = sorted(set(a["controls"].values()))
+    assert len(others) == 1
+    first = ("the swapped-mark recipe agrees on %d of %d matrices at the %s marks that annihilate their own line, and on %d of %d "
+             "at each of the other %s" % (a["row_test_equals_column_test_on_swapped"], a["matrices"], words[6 - len(a["controls"])],
+                                          others[0], a["matrices"], words[len(a["controls"])]))
+    second = ("the least reading is the all-ones' (√5/2), the second least the all-twos' (√2), and every other reads above 17/12, "
+              "the least of them 1.4866 at (1, 1, 2, 2)")
+    flat = " ".join(PAGE.split())
+    assert first in flat, first
+    assert second in flat, second
+    # planted: each of the five numbers changed on the page is reported now
+    for was, now in (("on 120 of 120", "on 119 of 120"), ("on 88 of 120", "on 87 of 120"), ("all-ones' (√5/2)", "all-ones' (√3/2)"),
+                     ("all-twos' (√2)", "all-twos' (√3)"), ("above 17/12", "above 16/12")):
+        assert was in flat
+        changed = flat.replace(was, now, 1)
+        assert first not in changed or second not in changed, was
+
